<!-- @before 4. Propagation Latency :: guide -->
### Measure reach instead of promising a fixed deadline

Push hints and refreshes do not guarantee delivery to offline or suspended clients. Preserve the last accepted safe state under the documented missing/fetch-failure policy, and observe actual activation and recovery. A live-safe control also needs authorization, validation and revision handling. [Remote Config loading strategies](https://firebase.google.com/docs/remote-config/loading).

<!-- @before 8. Kill Switches During A Bad Release :: staff -->
### Define what disabling can still stop

Blocking future starts, cancelling cooperative work and compensating a committed effect are separate operations. Give each worker a documented checkpoint/continuation policy. A client flag cannot revoke a server-side effect already accepted, so retain server authorization and compatibility controls.
